# vehje-runtime-driver. backlog

## Deferred loader implementation

- Real `dlopen` / `libloading` integration in
  `RuntimeLoader::load`. Currently returns
  `Err(LoaderError::NotImplemented)` regardless of path.
- Env-var convention. `CLAUSE_RUNTIME_PATH` points at the
  dylib. When unset, a conventional next-to-binary path is
  tried; when that fails, an embedded-fallback path is tried.
- Windows / Linux / macOS dylib naming conventions
  (`libvehje_runtime.{so,dylib,dll}`). the loader inspects
  the target triple and prepends / appends accordingly.
- Symbol resolution. `dlsym` each `extern "C"` entry by name;
  error with `LoaderError::SymbolNotFound { name }` on miss.
- ABI version check at load time. read the runtime's
  published `abi_version` and refuse on mismatch.

## Deferred handle implementation

- `DlopenHandle`. concrete `RuntimeHandle` impl backed by
  `libloading::Library`. Holds the library handle and
  function pointers resolved at load time.
- Handle lifecycle. drop closes the library via
  `libloading::Library::close` (implicit on drop).
- Multi-runtime management. load multiple runtime handles,
  route per-session.
- Per-session arena management. driver allocates / frees
  arenas through `vehje_runtime_init` /
  `vehje_runtime_shutdown`.

## Deferred driver features

- Real `RuntimeDriver` state. holds an `Arc<dyn RuntimeHandle>`
  + per-session cache of diagnostic translations.
- `AbiDiagnostic` → `vehje_ir::Diagnostic` conversion , 
  maps pointer-plus-length messages to `&'static str` or
  interned string ids.
- `AbiSpan` → `vehje_ir::Span` conversion. reconstructs
  `FileId` + `ByteOffset` from the flat triple.
- Fallback to embedded runtime when dylib not found , 
  statically-linked lightweight backend for test / dev use.
- Panic-at-FFI-boundary recovery. `catch_unwind` in the
  driver wrappers so a Zig-side abort surfaces as a
  `DriverError` instead of tearing down the process.

## Deferred vehje-schedule integration

- Macro-expansion pass. driver-backed pass in the schedule
  DAG that receives unit metadata and returns expanded nodes.
- Generative-expansion pass. driver-backed pass that expands
  generative subgraph blueprints into concrete nodes.
- Scratch-evaluation pass. compile-time expression folding
  via the driver.

## Non-blocking follow-ups

- Hot-reload of the runtime dylib during dev iteration.
- Per-runtime-version capability negotiation at load.
- Crash recovery. detect a crashed runtime handle and
  reinstall a fresh one.
